Brooo got it! ❤️ You want ALL 7 PROGRAMS (1a, 1b, 2a, 2b, 5a, 5b, 6a, 6b, 7a, 7b, 8a, 8b, 9a, 9b) and how to run each in VS Code without confusion.

I'll give you a common setup, exact filenames, commands, and expected outputs.

### Part 1: ExpressJS programs (1a, 1b, 2a, 2b)

### Step 1: Common setup

Open VS Code → create folder `ExpressLab` → open terminal.

Run:

```bash
npm init -y
npm install express ejs
```

Create these files:

```text
ExpressLab
│
├── 1a.js
├── 1b.js
├── 2a.js
├── 2b.js
└── views
    └── home.ejs
```

### Step 2: Run each program

| Program           | Command    | Browser URL         |
| ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------- |
| 1(a) Routes       | node 1a.js | localhost:3000      |
| 1(b) HTTP methods | node 1b.js | localhost:3000/data |
| 2(a) EJS          | node 2a.js | localhost:3000      |
| 2(b) Forms        | node 2b.js | localhost:3000      |

Important: Stop the previous program using `Ctrl + C` before running the next one.

For 1(b), test POST and DELETE using Thunder Client or Postman. A browser address bar only sends GET requests.

For 2(a), `home.ejs` must be inside the `views` folder.

### Part 2: ReactJS programs (5a, 5b, 6a, 6b, 7a, 7b, 8a)

### Step 1: Create React project

Open a new VS Code terminal and run:

```bash
npm create vite@latest ReactLab -- --template react
```

Then:

```bash
cd ReactLab
```

```bash
npm install
```

```bash
npm run dev
```

Open the URL shown in terminal, usually:

`http://localhost:5173`

### Step 2: Where to paste code

Open:

```text
ReactLab
 └── src
      └── App.jsx
```

Delete existing code in `App.jsx` and paste your required program.

| Question | Code to paste              |
| -------- | -------------------------- |
| 5(a)     | HTML rendering code        |
| 5(b)     | JSX code                   |
| 6(a)     | Props and state code       |
| 6(b)     | CSS/Sass code              |
| 7(a)     | Event handling code        |
| 7(b)     | Conditional rendering code |
| 8(a)     | List rendering code        |

For 6(b), also create `App.css` inside `src` and import it using:

```javascript
import './App.css';
```

To run: Keep `npm run dev` running. Save `App.jsx` after changing each program. The browser updates automatically.

You do not need to create seven separate React projects.

### Part 3: MongoDB programs (8b, 9a, 9b)

Run in MongoDB Shell – mongosh

These programs are NOT run using `node`. They are MongoDB commands.

### Step 1: Open MongoDB in VS Code

Open a new VS Code terminal and type:

```bash
mongosh
```

If successful, you'll see a MongoDB shell prompt similar to:

```text
test>
```

If MongoDB Server is installed as a Windows service but isn't running, open Command Prompt as Administrator and run:

```bash
net start MongoDB
```

Then return to VS Code and run `mongosh`.

If `mongosh` is not recognized, install MongoDB Shell separately; installing VS Code or Node.js alone does not install it.

### Step 2: Run each program

| Question      | Commands to execute                 |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| 8(b) CRUD     | Insert, find, update, remove        |
| 9(a) Database | use college and create/drop         |
| 9(b) Queries  | Find, limit, sort, index, aggregate |

### 8(b) CRUD

Paste each MongoDB query into `mongosh`:

```javascript
use college
```

```javascript
db.students.insert({name:"Monika", age:20})
```

```javascript
db.students.find()
```

```javascript
db.students.update(
{name:"Monika"},
{$set:{age:21}}
)
```

```javascript
db.students.remove({name:"Monika"})
```

### 9(a) Create and drop

```javascript
use college
```

```javascript
db.createCollection("students")
```

```javascript
show collections
```

```javascript
db.students.drop()
```

```javascript
db.dropDatabase()
```

### 9(b) MongoDB queries

```javascript
use college
```

```javascript
db.students.insertMany([
{name:"Monika",age:20,marks:90},
{name:"Ravi",age:21,marks:80},
{name:"Anu",age:19,marks:95}
])
```

Then execute:

```javascript
db.students.find()
```

```javascript
db.students.find().limit(2)
```

```javascript
db.students.find().sort({age:1})
```

```javascript
db.students.createIndex({name:1})
```

```javascript
db.students.aggregate([
{$group:{_id:null, avg:{$avg:"$marks"}}}
])
```

Expected: Three student records, limited records, sorted records, index creation confirmation and average marks of `88.33`.

